        "original_id": "7b483225-88cb-5a39-8fa5-4c276066b17f",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Ray Stark, Stanley Kubrick\n- Films: The World of Suzie Wong, West Side Story, The Misfits, Lolita, The Night of the Iguana, Reflections in a Golden Eye, Funny Girl, The Goodbye Girl, The Toy, Annie, Steel Magnolias\n- Roles: literary agent, theatrical agent, film producer, director\n- Topics: film career, 1960s films, 1970s films, 1980s films, 1990s films\n\nFacts:\n- Ray Stark’s background as a literary agent and theatrical agent helped prepare him to become a successful film producer.\n- Ray Stark produced The World of Suzie Wong, West Side Story, and The Misfits in 1961.\n- Stanley Kubrick directed Lolita, a 1962 British-American black comedy-drama film.\n- Ray Stark produced Lolita in 1962.\n- Ray Stark produced The Night of the Iguana in 1964, Reflections in a Golden Eye in 1967, and Funny Girl in 1968.\n- Ray Stark produced The Goodbye Girl in 1977.\n- Ray Stark produced The Toy and Annie in 1982.\n- Ray Stark produced Steel Magnolias in 1989.\n- Ray Stark produced dynamic and profitable films across the 1960s, 1970s, 1980s, and 1990s.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
